WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:04.931
EventWorld: Forecasting Future Geometry from Events Alone

2
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.454
At night, events reveal edges that RGB can miss.

3
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.578
Events still reveal edges during fast motion.

4
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.400
We use three past event packets.

5
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.686
Two frozen encoders capture structure and motion.

6
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.664
Geometry guides the fusion.

7
00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:30.917
One pass forecasts the future geometric state.

8
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:38.074
The frozen decoder outputs depth, point clouds, and camera poses.

9
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.175
We query each horizon directly from the same history.

10
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.877
On a city street, we show rolling forecasts at real-time playback speed.

11
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:04.465
At a bend on the bridge, the forecast updates as the vehicle turns.

12
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.291
For scene distances, EventWorld has the lowest depth error.

13
00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:16.285
Point clouds reveal the scene's layout.

14
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.674
The road and buildings remain recognizable.

15
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.245
Camera poses capture motion. Orange is predicted, blue is measured.

16
00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:31.514
In this night scene, EventWorld more than halves depth error.

17
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.842
EventWorld achieves lower depth error than both baselines.

18
00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.929
From past events to future geometry.
